    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d199">

                <pb facs="0648" n="607" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v24/pg607"/>

                <head>199. Memorandum From Director of Central Intelligence Turner to Vice President
                        Mondale<anchor n="1" xml:id="d199-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-sibling-dates" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1977-06-27T23:59:59-05:00"
                            notBefore="1977-06-27T00:00:00-05:00">undated</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Recent Activities of Eduardo Frei</item>
                </list>
                <p>1. Attached<anchor n="2" xml:id="d199-f2"/> is a memorandum on the recent
                    activities of the former President of Chile, Eduardo Frei. This might be of
                    particular interest to you in the light of your late May discussion with
                        him.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d199-f3"/></p>
                <p>This subject will also be treated in a forthcoming issue [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >less than 1 line not declassified</hi>].<anchor n="4" xml:id="d199-f4"
                    /></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#bold">Stansfield Turner</hi><anchor n="5"
                            xml:id="d199-f5"/></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d199-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d199-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Central Intelligence Agency, Office of the Director of Central
                    Intelligence, Job 80M00165A, Box 5, Folder 130: C-7: Chile. Secret. Drafted [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">less than 1 line not declassified</hi>] on July 1,
                    concurrence by Wells on July 2. Printed from a copy which indicates that it was
                    sent on July 5.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d199-f2" n="2" xml:id="d199-f2-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d200">Document 200</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d199-f3" n="3" xml:id="d199-f3-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d194">Document 194</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d199-f4" n="4" xml:id="d199-f4-content">
                <p>July 7, 1977. (Carter Library, National Security Affairs, Brzezinski Material,
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">less than 1 line not declassified</hi>] File, Box
                    3, 7/7/77-7/15/77)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d199-f5" n="5" xml:id="d199-f5-content">
                <p>A notation indicating that Turner signed the memorandum was typed above his
                    name.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
